From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 03:02:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] report an absent gpu_mem map instead of aborting

ReadPerProcessGpuMem and ReadProcessGpuUsageKb each contain a graceful path for
an unavailable map, and both are dead code. BpfMapRO calls abortOnMismatch
unconditionally from its constructor, and abortOnMismatch aborts as soon as the
fd is invalid, so isValid() can never observe a missing map.

The map is genuinely absent on this platform rather than misconfigured.
CONFIG_BPF_EVENTS depends on KPROBE_EVENTS or UPROBE_EVENTS, arch/um declares
neither HAVE_KPROBES nor ARCH_SUPPORTS_UPROBES, and the gpu_mem tracepoint
program that creates the map can never attach. Only the socket-filter object is
pinned under /sys/fs/bpf in a running guest.

The result was a fatal abort in system_server through
android_os_Debug_getGpuTotalUsageKb and MemInfoReader.getGpuKernelUsedSizeKb,
restarting the runtime before boot completed.

Check the pinned path before constructing the map in both functions so the
existing return false becomes reachable. Every framework caller already tests
Debug.getGpuTotalUsageKb() >= 0, so reporting the absence is the contract they
expect and is accurate: this product has no kernel GPU memory accounting.
---
 sysmeminfo.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sysmeminfo.cpp b/sysmeminfo.cpp
index c014987916efbe68b37421bea65ff538ab2a8d4f..38445e10cf891c22cf08b8facbf303e1485c37b8 100644
--- a/sysmeminfo.cpp
+++ b/sysmeminfo.cpp
@@ -415,6 +415,19 @@ bool ReadPerProcessGpuMem([[maybe_unused]] std::unordered_map<uint32_t, uint64_t
 #if defined(__ANDROID__) && !defined(__ANDROID_APEX__) && !defined(__ANDROID_VNDK__)
     static constexpr const char kBpfGpuMemTotalMap[] = "/sys/fs/bpf/map_gpuMem_gpu_mem_total_map";
 
+    // BpfMapRO aborts from its constructor when the pinned map is absent, so
+    // the isValid() guard below is only reachable when the path exists.
+    // Platforms that cannot load tracing BPF programs never pin this map:
+    // CONFIG_BPF_EVENTS requires KPROBE_EVENTS or UPROBE_EVENTS, and an
+    // architecture that provides neither can never attach the gpu_mem
+    // tracepoint program that creates it. Report the absence instead of
+    // aborting the caller; every framework caller already handles a negative
+    // result from Debug.getGpuTotalUsageKb().
+    if (access(kBpfGpuMemTotalMap, F_OK) != 0) {
+        LOG(ERROR) << "Not present: " << kBpfGpuMemTotalMap;
+        return false;
+    }
+
     // Use the read-only wrapper BpfMapRO to properly retrieve the read-only map.
     auto map = bpf::BpfMapRO<uint64_t, uint64_t>(kBpfGpuMemTotalMap);
     if (!map.isValid()) {
@@ -469,6 +482,19 @@ bool ReadProcessGpuUsageKb([[maybe_unused]] uint32_t pid, [[maybe_unused]] uint3
     // BPF Key [32-bits GPU ID | 32-bits PID]
     uint64_t kBpfKeyGpuUsage = ((uint64_t)gpu_id << 32) | pid;
 
+    // BpfMapRO aborts from its constructor when the pinned map is absent, so
+    // the isValid() guard below is only reachable when the path exists.
+    // Platforms that cannot load tracing BPF programs never pin this map:
+    // CONFIG_BPF_EVENTS requires KPROBE_EVENTS or UPROBE_EVENTS, and an
+    // architecture that provides neither can never attach the gpu_mem
+    // tracepoint program that creates it. Report the absence instead of
+    // aborting the caller; every framework caller already handles a negative
+    // result from Debug.getGpuTotalUsageKb().
+    if (access(kBpfGpuMemTotalMap, F_OK) != 0) {
+        LOG(ERROR) << "Not present: " << kBpfGpuMemTotalMap;
+        return false;
+    }
+
     // Use the read-only wrapper BpfMapRO to properly retrieve the read-only map.
     auto map = bpf::BpfMapRO<uint64_t, uint64_t>(kBpfGpuMemTotalMap);
     if (!map.isValid()) {
